        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d9e2273e-05e7-5b44-8693-8014bcbb40dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Rice; Leslie Marmon Silko; Elton John; Kenneth Lincoln\n- Works: \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight\"; Ceremony; The Lion King\n- Organizations: Disney; Penguin\n- Concepts: Native American Renaissance\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Rice was born on 10 November 1944 and is an English author and lyricist.\n- Leslie Marmon Silko was born on March 5, 1948 and is a Laguna Pueblo writer.\n- Ceremony is a novel by Leslie Marmon Silko that Penguin first published in March 1977.\n- \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight\" is a song from Disney's 1994 animated film The Lion King.\n- Elton John composed \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight,\" and Tim Rice wrote its lyrics.\n- Leslie Marmon Silko is one of the key figures in the First Wave of the Native American Renaissance, a term literary critic Kenneth Lincoln used.\n- Tim Rice has won Academy, Golden Globe, Tony, and Grammy awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
